it is friday and it's time for the  mailbag you can email info at  davidpakman.com if you have something to  say sometimes we'll look at tweets  sometimes we'll look at youtube comments  um could be from anywhere let's get  right into it first one today indeed  does come to us from youtube it's from  john john says david why won't you talk  about hunter biden's laptop you must  support russia  ukraine and china  david you are our shame well another  unintelligible screed very common to  youtube we've talked about hunter  biden's laptop as a media story probably  a handful of times and of course i must  support russia  and ukraine  and china  those are all players on different sides  of the game different perspectives i'm  starting to think that john may not be  fully versed in geopolitics  based on this message  michael wrote in about the fox news mass  shooting response and says hey david  curious as to how fox news and other  right-wing types could possibly believe  that prayer in church is the answer  when the u.s is 30th worldwide in  percentage of atheists and i know you  know where we rank in the world for mass  shootings i am sick of these people not  having any responsibility for the  nonsense they spew out on a daily basis  it makes me want to quit paying  attention to anything political  hope is gone yet with all of these  things there's always some absurdity  where all signs point to guns as at  least a major factor that has to be  dealt with oh we don't have enough  religion well we have way more religion  than most countries  and we also have way more shootings so  if you want to look at that correlation  it doesn't bode particularly well for  god maybe god just isn't a factor in  this one way or the other and it's time  to actually look at guns i don't know  just an idea but  mike from atlanta  accurately  pointing that out  kristoff wrote in and said can we talk  about the irony that the people who for  the past two years were crying about the  psychological effect that masks would  have on children at schools  now want children to wear ballistic  blankets in case of a shooting and watch  their teacher shoot someone in front of  them yeah the the it's actually  multi-layered  and i tweeted about some of these things  on the one hand  the covet masks were irreparably  psychologically traumatizing to the kids  but wearing you know a bulletproof  backpack a ballistic blanket and having  their teachers be armed  is supposed to not have a detrimental  psychological impact that obviously  makes no sense but there's also the  hypocrisy when it comes to the teachers  the these are the very teachers that the  right wing has spent the last two years  saying  uh these are groomers  these are people  perpetuating the psychological abuse by  enforcing mask rules they're  indoctrinators they are wokesters they  are critical race theory teaching  indoctrinators who can't be trusted  let's give them the ultimate  responsibility of being armed in school  so that they can take out mass shooters  wait you've just said they're not even  capable of choosing the books your kids  should learn from and now you want to  give them guns it's completely absurd  and kristoff accurately points it out  anthony wrote in about the texas school  shooting  and says i thought your piece on the  texas school shooting was quite good  with one exception you didn't have time  to question how hardening the schools  with weapons is going to take care of  the movie theaters and grocery stores  and churches and all the other places  crazy people decide to go and shoot  people for fun how would the right wing  gun toting bible beating right to life  or solve that otherwise excellent work  david that's anthony from sag harbor  yeah this is a point that i made during  a live stream but anthony's right i  missed this during during our podcast  segment which is  even if you did all the stuff they want  to do at schools and even if it worked  which of course it's like they don't  want to deal with the gun part but  imagine you did it all  you can't do it at a ton of these other  establishments that have had shootings  you can't do it at the grocery stores  for practical purposes you can't do it  at the movie theaters  it's um  now  it's fair to say we need different  solutions to different problems that's  absolutely fine but again at some point  you've got to deal with the guns you're  not going to have solutions to all these  things without ever dealing with the  guns which is exactly what they want to  do  samuel wrote in about marcus flowers  um okay this this is an important email  samuel says david sir i applaud you for  recommending campaign involvement to  your audience but i really caution  against sending uh sending excess time  and donations to marcus flowers campaign  i worry too many progressives will make  the same mistake they made with the amy  mcgrath campaign in 2020  out of a passion to oust mitch mcconnell  only to see her lose big time  instead i would recommend efforts going  towards flippable races tim ryan in ohio  beasley in north carolina fetterman and  pennsylvania  and defending vulnerable incumbents  spanberger in virginia and slotkin in  michigan the truth there simply aren't  enough democratic voters to oust green  something something i obviously want to  see happen someday  in that district and the primary numbers  from wednesday reflect that in my  judgment it's better to keep green and  the minority then naively assume  we can remove her at this time this is a  completely fair point i'm never going to  say  ignore this race okay  but it is absolutely true  that the numbers in marjory taylor  green's district make it hard to believe  that in such a red district the  non-incumbent democratic nominee  flowers  is going to be able to win  now i'm not saying ignore the race but  we do have limited resources and i think  samuel makes an important point here  about understanding how to best use  those admittedly limited resources  keep it in mind  uh okay hannah wrote in and says  recession soon  hi david i'm hearing more news stories  that say the u.s is barreling toward  recession right now and that this  recession will start within the next  year do you agree why or why not thank  you hannah here's the difficulty of this  question  we may already be in a recession we may  be getting out of it right now we you  know  everybody defines it differently  understand that for a decade many have  been saying a recession is imminent uh  around 2015 there were lots of people  saying a recession is imminent imagine  if you had listened to them in 2015 and  said i believe the recession is imminent  i'm getting out of the stock market you  would have missed one of the greatest  run-ups in the stock market in decades  so my view is i don't know if a  recession is coming i can't control  whether a recession is coming at some  point there will be another recession  what do i know well i know my principles  i know that my principle is asset  allocation and my principle is low-cost  index funds without trying to time the  market and my principle is when the  market goes down  those same index fund purchases get me  more shares at a lower price because i  can't time it i don't know whether a  recession is coming and so i think a lot  of times the right question to ask is if  a recession were coming what what would  i do or what would i do differently  for most people the answer is well  actually nothing i wouldn't do anything  differently so i don't have the answer  uh about a recession but what i do have  is a plan  that is the plan whether or not we are  in a recession i hope that makes sense  niels wrote in with an idea for  when we get to 1.5 million youtube  subscribers and neil says hi david on  achieving 1.5 million subscribers may i  suggest you receive a colonoscopy on air  so  the joke here is recently  someone wrote in and said david you  should do a colonoscopy when you get to  1.5 million subscribers and the wording  was funny because typically it's the  doctors doing the the uh colonoscopy and  it's the patients receiving so i was  like are you saying that i should  receive one or that i should perform one  niels is clarifying that and saying i  should receive the colonoscopy when i  get to 1.5 million subscribers well  that's something we will look into okay  lucas has a different idea lucas says  hello david love your show i've been  watching the last two years now watching  your show reading suggestions for what  to do for 1.5 million on youtube i think  you should eat a carolina reaper it is  the world's hottest pepper and i feel  like it would gather a lot of attention  to your channel you should also set a  date for when you want to hit it in  order to eat the pepper i'm just going  to pass on that i am not interested in  hot peppers  uh i mean listen i love a good jalapeno  i'll use fresno chilies and cooking  dried thai chilies serrano for a  beautiful coconut cod chowder that i  like to make you chop up a serrano  pepper it's beautiful smoky heat  but i don't like stunts like this i  don't like eating contests and i have no  this is a no this is a hard no i would  sooner bleacher my hair or shave my head  than uh than do do this stacy wrote in  does a fetus have a right to get child  support  hi  if life begins at conception  shouldn't child support start at  conception yours stacy i've brought this  up many times before  um  the issue  about personhood at conception raises  really important questions  um if a fetus is a citizen  if a fetus is a person at conception  then it is a citizen right i mean it  should be able to be made a citizen  and even if it's the fetus of an  undocumented immigrant they should be  able to get citizenship  after conception because if it's a  person people get citizenship  if it is a person at conception then  presumably it would be entitled to child  support as well  uh it i mean listen  good luck actually having rational  conversations about these things with  the anti-choice movement but of course  stacy brings up a good point which is  it's less about when do we say life has  started  forms of life exist in so many places  and in so many ways and a fetus is less  about whether it qualifies as quote life  but  what is a person and what are the rights  that come with personhood because the  anti-choice movement wants to to talk a  lot about specific rights that they  believe a fetus should have  but not about many of the others that  people persons  also get  and it's an age-old hypocrisy as long as  roe v wade has been around all of these  arguments have been around and sadly  they very often become philosophical  black holes and you don't get anywhere  with them but an important question  info davidpakman.com if you have  questions comments suggestions that you  would like featured in the weekly  mailbag make sure that you are signed up  at  joinpackman.com get a membership get the  bonus show and get the commercial free  audio and video feeds of the show  every day  six hours before  they are published to everybody  joinpakman.com is the place to sign up

